    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0073" n="69" xml:id="pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.04/12313: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-04T23:00:00+00:00">February 4, 1938—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 4—6:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Mr. Hugh Wilson<anchor n="3" xml:id="d81-f1"/> informs me that, when talking
                    privately with Mr. Eden for a moment this afternoon, Mr. Eden told him that if
                    the Japanese attacked Hong Kong they would act at once in its defense; that this
                    might mean the withdrawal of substantial forces from the Mediterranean but that
                    the British could not do otherwise. He further said that the British would act
                    to defend Hong Kong if attacked regardless of what American action might be.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d81-f1" n="3" xml:id="d81-f1-content">
                <p>Newly appointed Ambassador to Germany.</p>
            </note>
